# Rust Async Roof Angle Calculation Service

Async microservice on Rust that accepts a POST request with roofing materials and load data, immediately returns HTTP 200, then asynchronously calculates optimal tilt angles for each material and sends results back to the main backend via a callback endpoint.

## Proposed Changes

### Project Initialization

#### [NEW] [Cargo.toml](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/Cargo.toml)

Rust project manifest with dependencies: `tokio`, `reqwest`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `dotenv`, `actix-web`, `rand`.

#### [NEW] [.env](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/.env)

Environment config:
- `HOST` — server host (default `localhost`)
- `LISTEN_PORT` — server port (default `8083`)
- `ASYNC_TOKEN` — secret key sent in callback
- `CALLBACK_BASE_URL` — base URL of the main backend (default `http://localhost:8080`)

---

### Data Models

#### [NEW] [models.rs](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/src/models.rs)

Structs:
- `RoofingMaterial` — input material with `id: i64`, `min_angle: i32`, `max_angle: i32`
- `CalcRequest` — incoming request body: `snow_load: Option<i32>`, `wind_load: Option<i32>`, `materials: Vec<RoofingMaterial>`
- `MaterialResult` — per-material result: `id: i64`, `optimal_angle: i32`
- `CallbackPayload` — callback body sent to the main backend: `async_token: String`, `results: Vec<MaterialResult>`

---

### Calculation Logic

#### [NEW] [calculation.rs](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/src/calculation.rs)

- `calculate_optimal_angle(snow_load, wind_load, material) -> i32` — implements the formula: `max(α_min, min(α_max, arctan((Sg/200)*(W0/50)) + (2/7)*α_min))`. Returns midpoint `(min+max)/2` if loads are `None`.
- `calculate_all(req: &CalcRequest) -> Vec<MaterialResult>` — iterates over all materials and calculates angle for each.
- Unit tests with `#[cfg(test)]` module.

---

### HTTP Handlers

#### [NEW] [handlers.rs](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/src/handlers.rs)

- `POST /api/roof_angle_calculation/{id}/finish` handler:
  1. Parses `id` from URL path and body as `CalcRequest`
  2. Returns `200 OK` with `{"message": "Data received successfully"}` immediately
  3. Spawns async task via `tokio::spawn` that:
     - Calls `calculate_all` to compute results
     - Sleeps 5–10 seconds (`rand::thread_rng().gen_range(5..=10)`)
     - Sends PUT to `{CALLBACK_BASE_URL}/api/roof_angle_calculation/{id}/callback` with `CallbackPayload`
- `init(cfg)` — registers the route

---

### Server Setup

#### [NEW] [server.rs](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/src/server.rs)

- `Settings` struct loaded from env: `host`, `port`, `async_token`, `callback_base_url`
- `start_server(settings)` — launches actix-web HttpServer

#### [NEW] [main.rs](file:///Users/l.poljakov/Documents/BMSTU/Development%20of%20internet%20applications/Development-of-Internet-Applications-Async-Service/async_service/src/main.rs)

Entry point: loads settings, starts server.

